	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13506"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1" title="View the profile of Kinladar">Kinladar</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Ranger Bait<br />
								Administrator<br />
								Veeshan<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 14456<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/macross.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13506#msg13506"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13506#msg13506">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #61 on:</b> January 03, 2005, 09:03:22 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I think releasing content before all aspects are finished is an industry wide problem for MMORPG&#039;s in general. Haven&#039;t heard of, or seen one yet that came with it all at the begining like promised. Not EQ, Not WoW, none of them have been able to.<br /><br />Doesn&#039;t make it right, but that&#039;s the sad reality in that the investors want to see a return sooner than what the developers are ever ready to deliver. Since the investors write the checks, the devs are forced to be the ones to compromise. It&#039;s how they come to that stage is what matters. I don&#039;t mind personally waiting for the final touches to be put on if the quality is maintained. So far WoW has kept to that aspect at least, SoE however has yet to deliver once.<br /><br />My main thoughts on game design boil down to the idiocy of the flagging systems, and how they were built to just keep people out of the good zones.<br /><br />Worst&nbsp; Idea&nbsp; Ever<br /><br />All it did was drive a wedge in the EQ community. The flagging systems, and added in lack of small group quests, and solo content dwindling over time, if not out right squashed by SoE devs at times in regards to soloing, is what has killed the game.<br /><br />When you take away options, you take away fun.<br /><br />Should SoE wake up, and make some fundamental changes to the game that would include allowing fear kiting again for those classes with fear spells, allow the Warriors, Rogues, Monks, and Zerkers places, and content that is designed for them to be able to solo, and such. Give the Priest classes in the Clerics, and Shaman more options once again to solo, (druids have always been able to find something to solo, so don&#039;t take that as a negative ommission, just that I think Clerics, and Shaman could use some areas for themselves.) Give places/abilities that Rangers, Bards, Paladins, Beastlords and SK&#039;s can solo effectively as well.<br /><br />SoE needs to wake up to the realization that the enforced grouping that they wanted to stick down everyone&#039;s throats so badly is what has been killing EQ for the last couple of years, and has simply led up to today. EQ2, and WoW were not the things that caused people to want to leave in Droves, EQ by itself, and by design has been driving people away for the last two years quite nicely, EQ2, and WoW just have given people more options is all.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.wowrankings.com/viewb.htm?name=Kinladar&amp;s_id=38" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/sig-kinladar-wow.jpg" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><a href="http://www.chaoticdiscord.org" target="_blank">Chaotic Discord</a> found in {World of Warcraft}<br />Guild Leader of Fires of Time (Retired)
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13508"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
